{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795780062,"nonce":"QwEa3kh8/DJH5cSvPs2ia9cvnF4=","title":"Plugin Pods, the isolation probe's Pods and the self-check initContainer get no tolerations or nodeSelector. On a cluster where every node is tainted they stay Pending, and no plugin can start.","message":"Found 2026-11-27 setting up the Argo CD plugin in tools-common: every node there is tainted (Karpenter pools `workload-type=\u003ctier\u003e:NoSchedule`, the managed node group `CriticalAddonsOnly`). Today the only workaround is an admission mutation (their Kyverno default-toleration policy).\n\nThe chart already places the server (`tolerations` / `nodeSelector`), the Data Depot (`workspace.*`) and step Pods (`scarab.placement`), but has nothing for plugins.\n\nChange:\n- chart: `plugins.tolerations` (list) and `plugins.nodeSelector` (map), default empty;\n- server: one env var `SCARAB_PLUGIN_PLACEMENT` (JSON `{tolerations, nodeSelector}`), parsed and checked at boot;\n- runtime: set them on every plugin Deployment's Pod template and on the three probe Pods, so the probe tests the nodes plugins run on.\n\nOperator-set only; a plugin manifest cannot ask for placement.","files":null}]}